---
/**
 * The how-it-works deck, lifted.
 *
 * public/how-it-works.html is a self-contained page: its own markup, its own
 * stylesheet, its own script. It is placed here unchanged.
 *
 * A previous attempt "lifted" it by scoping every selector under .hiw,
 * prefixing its keyframes, stripping its script and rewiring its navigation to
 * :target. That is a rewrite, and it produced a deck missing its artefacts and
 * its rail — because once you are editing it, you are responsible for every
 * piece you did not carry across. A frame carries all of them, because it
 * carries the page.
 *
 * It also settles the collisions for free. That page and home.css both define
 * .card, .field, .rail, .btn and .logo; in a frame they cannot reach each
 * other, so neither has to be renamed.
 *
 * What comes with it: the deck runs its own script, so this section — and only
 * this section — depends on JavaScript. The rest of the page still ships none.
 * That is the deck's existing limitation travelling with the deck, and the fix
 * belongs in that file rather than in a copy of it.
 */
---

<section class="hiw" id="how">
  <iframe
    src="/how-it-works.html"
    title="How it works — step by step"
    loading="lazy"
  ></iframe>
</section>

<style>
  .hiw {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--void);
  }
  .hiw iframe {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    /* The deck lays itself out against the viewport, so the frame has to give
       it a viewport-shaped box or its own clamps collapse. */
    height: min(860px, 92vh);
    min-height: 620px;
    border: 0;
  }
</style>
